  (subsection function-editor
   (doc "Load, edit, and save a binding's AST from the UI")
   (status partial)
   (verify
    (build "dune build image")
    (smoke "POST /edit/editor-greet save -> callable via /api/eval")
    (smoke "GET /edit/missing-fn shows create affordance, not silent TODO only")
    (smoke "GET /edit/hello after hello-recipe: offers Edit hi-page + Create hello")
    (smoke "htmx POST create missing fn returns editor partial; save works"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         URL: /edit/<function-name>  (function name, NEVER a route path
         as the object of edit — routes are pages).

         v1 SHIPPED: plain textarea editor + save on current branch
         when the binding already exists.

         REQUIRED NEXT — missing binding empty state:
         When GET /edit/<name> and no function_defs row for name:

         1. Do NOT present only a raw TODO stub as if the user is
            already editing a real function.

         2. Show an explicit card:
              Function "<name>" does not exist.

         3. Route awareness: if a page route "/<name>" (or path
            equal to name) exists with handler H:
              There is a page /<name> that currently runs function H.
              Primary:  [ Edit H ]  -> /edit/H
              Secondary:[ Create function <name> ]
              Optional: [ Create <name> and point /<name> at it ]
                (define + route update; power move)
            If no such route: only Create (and link back to Functions).

         4. Create-in-place via htmx (no full-page dead end):
              POST /api/edit/create  {name}  (and optional rebind_route)
              -> 200 HTML partial: the editor form for the new binding
                 (same fields as GET /edit/<name> after create)
              hx-target=#editor-root hx-swap=innerHTML
              Default body stub:
                (lambda ()\n  "TODO: implement <name>")
              After create, user saves via existing POST /edit/<name>.

         5. Creating a function does not silently rename routes unless
            the user chose "point page at it".

         6. Namespaced names (image.packages):
            - Accept full names with `/` (todo/list) in name field.
            - Create form MAY split package + local name and join with `/`.
            - URL routing for /edit/todo/list: either path segments after
              /edit/ joined back to todo/list, or /edit?name=todo%2Flist.
              Prefer path join if http router is easy; document choice.

         DEFERRED: optimistic concurrency / stale-body reject,
         structural AST tree-editor (branching.ast-nodes).
    |))
   )
  )
  (subsection inspector
   (doc "Inspect values, rows, ASTs, and page→function graphs live")
   (status partial)
   (verify
    (build "dune build image")
    (smoke "GET /inspect/binding/<name> shows author + AST")
    (smoke "GET /page/hello after recipe: handler hi-page listed")
    (smoke "page inspector lists callees of handler when body calls other fns"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         v1 SHIPPED: binding AST pretty+JSON; data row JSON pretty.

         REQUIRED NEXT — page → functions graph:
         GET /page/<path> (also linked from /pages "inspect"):

         A. Routing panel
            - Page URL (canonical route key)
            - Handler function name
            - Links: open page, edit handler, change handler (deferred UI)

         B. Functions this page uses (STATIC analysis)
            - Always include the handler as root
            - Walk handler body AST; collect App heads that are Vars
              naming a visible function_def on the current branch
            - Depth: transitive closure of user bindings (cap depth
              e.g. 8 to avoid cycles; mark cycles)
            - Do not list pure prims as first-class rows; optional
              dim note "also uses prims: render-html, ..." is OK
            - Each row: name, role (handler|callee), edit + inspect links

         C. Entry body
            - Pretty source or pp_expr of the handler (read-only here;
              edit goes to /edit/<handler>)

         This answers: "which functions does this endpoint touch?"

         REVERSE INDEX (function → pages) — now REQUIRED for the
         Functions browser (system-browser), not only deferred:
         - For each visible route, compute handler + static callee set.
         - Invert to map function-name -> list of route keys.
         - Expose on /bindings rows as "used by" links to /page/<path>.
         - Same static analysis as page inspector (no runtime traces).

         DEFERRED: eval-result inspect, type-def deep inspect,
         runtime request traces, mutate actions from inspector.
    |))
   )
  )
 )

